<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Gorges</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1618–1670</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Gorges (1618–1670) was an English lawyer and a cousin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinando-gorges">Sir Ferdinando Gorges</a>, proprietor of the Province of Maine. He served as deputy governor of the province from 1640 to 1643, holding courts and organising government in Ferdinando's absence, and was mayor of the new city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">Gorgeana</a> (York). He then returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and sided with Parliament in the Civil War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-gorges.jpg" alt="Thomas Gorges" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SirThomasGorges_Died1610_OfLongfordCastle_Wiltshire.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
